      "content": "# CompTIA A+ Deep Dive - Complete Study Guide Index\n\n> Built from a full read of all 22 module decks (A220-1201 M01-M10, A220-1202 M11-M22), all 34 labs, the video library, and the existing `CompTIA_A_Plus_Mastery` files. This folder goes several layers deeper than the 00-09 files one level up. Use those as the quick-recall layer and these as the actual learning layer.\n\n## How the two exams split\n\n| Exam | Code | Files in this folder | Domains (weight) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Core 1** | 220-1201 | 02-16 | Mobile Devices 15% · Networking 20% · Hardware 25% · Virtualization & Cloud 11% · HW/Network Troubleshooting 29% |\n| **Core 2** | 220-1202 | 17-32 | Operating Systems 31% · Security 25% · Software Troubleshooting 22% · Operational Procedures 22% |\n\nBoth: max 90 questions, 90 minutes, includes performance-based questions (PBQs). Passing: Core 1 = 675/900, Core 2 = 700/900.\n\n## File map\n\n### Foundations\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 01 | [Exam Blueprint & Strategy](01_Exam_Blueprint_and_Strategy.md) | - |\n| 02 | [Troubleshooting Methodology](02_Troubleshooting_Methodology.md) | M01 |\n\n### Core 1 - Hardware\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 03 | [Cables, Connectors & Peripherals](03_Cables_Connectors_Peripherals.md) | M02 |\n| 04 | [Motherboards & Expansion Cards](04_Motherboards_Expansion_Cards.md) | M02 |\n| 05 | [Power Supplies & Cooling](05_Power_Supplies_Cooling.md) | M03 |\n| 06 | [Storage Devices & RAID](06_Storage_and_RAID.md) | M03 |\n| 07 | [RAM & CPUs](07_RAM_and_CPUs.md) | M03 |\n| 08 | [BIOS/UEFI & Hardware Troubleshooting](08_BIOS_UEFI_Hardware_Troubleshooting.md) | M04 |\n\n### Core 1 - Networking\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 09 | [Network Types, Hardware & Cabling](09_Network_Types_Hardware_Cabling.md) | M05 |\n| 10 | [Wireless Networking](10_Wireless_Networking.md) | M05 |\n| 11 | [Internet Connections, TCP/IP & Addressing](11_Internet_Connections_TCPIP_Addressing.md) | M06 |\n| 12 | [Ports, Protocols & Network Services](12_Ports_Protocols_Network_Services.md) | M06, M07 |\n| 13 | [DHCP, DNS, VLANs, VPNs & Network Troubleshooting](13_DHCP_DNS_VLAN_VPN_Network_Troubleshooting.md) | M06, M07 |\n\n### Core 1 - Virtualization, Mobile, Printers\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 14 | [Virtualization & Cloud](14_Virtualization_and_Cloud.md) | M08 |\n| 15 | [Mobile Devices & Laptops](15_Mobile_Devices_and_Laptops.md) | M09 |\n| 16 | [Printers & Multifunction Devices](16_Printers.md) | M10 |\n\n### Core 2 - Operating Systems\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 17 | [Support Procedures, Professionalism & OS Types](17_Support_Procedures_Professionalism_OS_Types.md) | M11 |\n| 18 | [Windows Settings & Configuration](18_Windows_Settings_and_Configuration.md) | M12 |\n| 19 | [Windows Management Consoles & CLI](19_Windows_Management_Consoles_and_CLI.md) | M13 |\n| 20 | [Windows Networking & Network Troubleshooting Tools](20_Windows_Networking_and_Troubleshooting_Tools.md) | M13, M14 |\n| 21 | [Remote Access, Performance Tools & OS Troubleshooting](21_Remote_Access_Performance_OS_Troubleshooting.md) | M14 |\n| 22 | [Windows Security, Accounts, Shares & Permissions](22_Windows_Security_Accounts_Shares_Permissions.md) | M15 |\n| 23 | [Windows Editions & OS Installation](23_Windows_Editions_and_OS_Installation.md) | M16 |\n| 24 | [Linux](24_Linux.md) | M17 |\n| 25 | [macOS](25_macOS.md) | M17 |\n\n### Core 2 - Security\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 26 | [Threats, Attacks & Social Engineering](26_Threats_Attacks_Social_Engineering.md) | M18 |\n| 27 | [Wireless Security & SOHO Router Hardening](27_Wireless_Security_SOHO_Router_Hardening.md) | M18 |\n| 28 | [Physical Security](28_Physical_Security.md) | M18 |\n| 29 | [Workstation & Browser Security, Malware Removal](29_Workstation_Browser_Security_Malware.md) | M19 |\n| 30 | [Mobile OS Security & Troubleshooting](30_Mobile_Security_and_Troubleshooting.md) | M20 |\n\n### Core 2 - Operational Procedures\n| # | File | Source modules |\n|---|---|---|\n| 31 | [Backup, Data Handling & AI](31_Backup_Data_Handling_AI.md) | M21 |\n| 32 | [Change Management, Safety, Environment & Scripting](32_Change_Management_Safety_Environment_Scripting.md) | M22 |\n\n### Cross-cutting\n| # | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| 33 | [All 34 Labs - Detailed Walkthrough](33_Labs_Detailed_Walkthrough.md) | Every lab, what it teaches, what to type |\n| 34 | [Master Recall Tables](34_Master_Recall_Tables.md) | Every memorisation table in one place |\n| 35 | [Practice Questions with Answers](35_Practice_Questions.md) | 120 questions, exam style, explained |\n| 36 | [Datacentre Capstone Track](36_Datacentre_Capstone_Track.md) | The Checklist-project.docx, decoded |\n| 37 | [Glossary](37_Glossary.md) | Every acronym in the course |\n\n## How to use this folder\n\n1. **Day 0:** watch all 22 videos at 1.5× (≈90 min). Don't take notes.\n2. **Per topic:** read the DEEP_DIVE file → close it → answer the \"Self-Test\" questions at the bottom of each file out loud → reopen and check.\n3. **Daily:** 15 minutes on [34_Master_Recall_Tables](34_Master_Recall_Tables.md). Ports every single day.\n4. **Weekends:** labs on a throwaway VM (file 33).\n5. **Before each exam:** [35_Practice_Questions](35_Practice_Questions.md), then the one-level-up `09_CHEAT_SHEET`.\n\nSit Core 1 first. Do not interleave.\n",
