      "content": "1\nBIOs and UEFI\nChapter 5\n2\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 5.01\nWhat is BIOs?\nBIOS programming e nables interaction with motherboard before OS loads\nBIOS is sto red in nonvo latile media, thus called firmware\nPOST routines are built into firmware\nThe System Setup utility is also part of the firmware\n3\nLower 3rds\nBasic Input/Output System (BIOS)\nUnified Extensible Firmware Interface \n(UEFI) \nBIOS = Firmware\nMain BIOS (M_BIOS)\nBackup BIOS (B-BIOS)\n4\nLower 3rds\nBIOS performs the tasks that start up a \nPC\nPower-On Self-Test (POST)\nBIOS utility\nUEFI interface: keyboard shortcuts, \nSettings app, command prompt\n5\nLower 3rds\nBIOS/UEFI configuration settings utility\nTrusted Platform Module (TPM)\nFan control / Temperature monitoring settings\nremove the CMOS battery\nPress PC’s on/off button for 10 sections\nComplementary Metal -Oxide-Semiconductor \n(CMOS)\n6\nBIOS Chips\nM_BIOS\n• Active BIOS chip\nB_BIOS\n• Contains factory defaults\n\n7\n\n8\nCMOS Chip\nConstantly powered by its battery\nRetains data even when the PC is \npowered off\nSaves configuration settings of the PC\n\n9\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 5.02\n10\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 5.03\nSystem Setup\nSee Next Page\n11\nObjectives\n•220-1201 - Given a scenario, install and configure motherboards, central \nprocessing units (CPUs), and add -on cards .\no BIOS/Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) settings\n▪ Boot options\n▪ USB permissions\n▪ Trusted Platform Module (TPM) security features\n▪ Fan considerations\n▪ Secure Boot\n▪ Boot password\n▪ BIOS password\n•220-1202 - 2.7 Given a scenario, apply workstation security options and hardening \ntechniques.\no Basic input/output system (BIOS)/Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) \npasswords\n12\nLower 3rds\nNew BIOS called UEFI\nWe call it UEFI BIOS\nPress Del key to enter Setup Menu\nF12 to enter Boot Menu\nBoot options\n13\nLower 3rds\nUSB permissions\nTrusted Platform Module (TPM) security \nfeatures\nFan considerations\nSecure Boot\nBoot password\nBIOS password\n14\nLower 3rds\nAdministrator password / User password\nF2 or Delete\nwe can control all of this\nMake sure that you're aware of it\n15\n\n16\n\n17\n\n18\n\n19\nChipset tab\n\n20\nBoot tab\n\n21\nBoot tab\n22\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 5.04\nTroubleshooting Firmware\n23\nSystem Setup Screen",
