      "content": "1\nUsers, Groups, \nand Permissions\nChapter 13\n2\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 13.01\nNTFS Permissions\n3\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a Folder\nFull Control - Enables you to do anything you want.\n4\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a Folder\nModify- Enables you to read, write, and delete both files \nand subfolders.\n5\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a Folder\nRead and Execute - Enables you to see contents of the \nfolder and any subfolders as well as run any executable \nprograms or associations in the folder.\n6\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a Folder\nList Folder Contents - Enables you to see contents of the \nfolder and any subfolders.\n7\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a Folder\nRead - Enables you to view a folder’s contents and open \nany file in the folder.\n8\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a Folder\nWrite - Enables you to write files and create new \nfiles and folders.\n9\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 13.07\nSecurity Permissions\n10\nLower 3rds\nOBJ - Disable guest account\nOBJ - Apply account expiration dates\n11\nLower 3rds\nUser account management\nWhen the expiration date arrives, the \naccount is automatically disabled\ndisabling Autorun\ndisabling unused services\nThis feature can be disabled in one of \nthree ways: on the Settings menu, with \na Group Policy setting, or editing the \nRegistry. \n12\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a File\nFull Control - Enables you to do anything you want \nto the file.\n13\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a File\nModify- Enables you to read, write, and delete the file.\n14\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a File\nRead and Execute - Enables you to open and run the file.\n15\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a File\nRead - Enables you to open and view the contents\nof a file.\n16\nNTFS Permission Attributes for a File\nWrite - Enables you to open and write to the file.",
