      "content": "2\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 27.05\nInstalling a Local Printer\n3.7 Given a scenario, deploy and configure \nmultifunction devices/printers and settings.\n3\nL3s\n• Local printer setup ​\n• Objective term - Network printer setup \nvia Ethernet cable or wireless​\n• Objective term - USB​\n• Objective term - Serial​\n• Objective term - Be careful when \nunboxing any device​\n4\nL3s\n• Objective term - Most operating systems will \nautomatically install the correct printer \ndrivers (or you can find them on the printer's \nwebsite)\n• Firmware updates​\n• Spooler​\n• Objective term - Most printers have options \nfor print quality, size, color mode, tray \nsettings, orientation, etc.\n5\nL3s\n• Collate​\n• Objective term - Duplex​\n• Objective term - If multiple pages are stuck in \nthe queue, you can cancel printing in the spooler\n• Objective term - Changes to the spooler require \nadmin permissions​\n• Virtual printer​\n• Print to PDF, Print to XPS, Print to OneNote\n6\nL3s\n• OBJ term- PostScript (PS) or Printer \nControl Language (PCL) printer​\n7\nPostScript (PS)\nPostScript Language\n• Device independent\n• Print imaging method on \nnumerous printers\nPS Printers\n• Typically preferred \n- Graphics quality\n- Print consistency\n8\nPostScript (PS)\nImage source: http://www.paulbourke.net/dataformats/postscript/\n9\nPrinter Control \nLanguage (PCL)\nPrinter Control Language\n• Machine dependent\n- Matched to the computer’s OS\n• Encodes a document with the \nactions the printer is to use\n• Drawback\n- Diverse manufacturers may interpret \nthe PCL coding differently\n- Printed product may appear different\n10\nPrinter Control \nLanguage (PCL)\n\n11\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 27.06\nSharing Printers\n3.7 Given a scenario, deploy and configure \nmultifunction devices/printers and settings.\n12\nL3s\n• Objective term - Share printer​\n• Objective term - Print server​\n• Objective term - Use appropriate \ndrivers for a given OS\n• Objective term - Shared printer \nsecurity settings​\n13\nL3s\n• Objective term - Printers shared on a domain \nhave to be set up with the domain users​\n• Mapping a printer​\n• Data privacy​\n• Objective term - User authentication​\n• Objective term- Badging\n• Objective term- Audit logs\n• Objective term- Secured prints\n14\nL3s\n• Controlling who can print can involve \nseveral types of authentication\n15\nPrinter Security\nBadging\n• ID badge, cards, and tokens\n- User’s identity and authorization\n• Require physical action\nCompromised printers\n• Generate audit and event \nrecords\n- Log files scanned\n16\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 27.07\nInstalling Wireless and Cloud \nPrinters\n3.7 Given a scenario, deploy and configure \nmultifunction devices/printers and settings.\n17\nL3s\n• Objective term - Wired (Ethernet) \nconnection​\n• Mac - SLP, Windows - LLDP​\n• Ad hoc (wireless network)​\n• Bluetooth​\n• Zeroconf (Zero configuration) - Windows​\n• Bonjour - Mac​\n18\nL3s\n• AirPrint - wireless​\n• Objective term - Network scan services: \nSend to OneDrive, e-mail, cloud services, \netc.\n• Objective term - Cloud printing via \nGoogle Cloud Print\n• Multi-function printer (MFP) device \n19\nMFP Devices\nMFP devices can provide document \nscanning services to network users\nMultiple MFP connections\n• Three choices\n- Email - Devices are set up to email \na document \n- Network - Users share access to printers, \nfile servers, ports, and other devices\n- Cloud - Provides cloud locations to receive \nprinting, scans, and copies\n20\nEpisode \ntitle:\nObjective:\nEpisode 27.08\nTroubleshooting Printers\n5.6 Given a scenario, troubleshoot printer issues\n21\nL3s\n• Unable to install a printer​\n• No connectivity​\n• Rollback device driver​\n• Access denied​\n• No image on printer display​\n• Objective term - Paper trouble! Paper not \nfeeding, paper/staple jam, issues with hole \npunches, multipage misfeed, etc.\n22\nL3s\n• Low memory errors​\n• Error code​\n• Objective term - Garbled characters on \npaper​\n• Objective term - Vertical lines on page​\n• Objective term - Color prints in the wrong \nprint color/incorrect color settings​\n• Printing blank pages​\n23\nL3s\n• Objective term - Streaks/speckling on \nprinted pages​\n• Objective term - Faded prints​\n• Objective term - Ghost images or \ndouble/echo images on the print​\n• Objective term - Toner not fused to \nprinter​\n• Creased paper​\n24\nL3s\n• OBJ Term- Grinding noises\n• OBJ Term- Unrecognized paper trays\n• OBJ Term- Connectivity issues\n• OBJ Term- Frozen print queue\n25\nGrinding Noises\nCauses\n• Carriage jam\n• Paper jam\n• Bad printer driver\nSolutions\n• Reset printer\n• Run troubleshooting software\n• Update the printer driver\n• Clear carriage or paper jams\n26\nUnrecognized Paper \nTrays\nCauses\n• Alignment Issue\n• Check for debris\n• Paper wrong size\nSolutions\n• Remove the tray, then fully insert it\n• Make sure the paper is the \ncorrect size\n• Check the printer settings\n27\nConnectivity\nCauses\n• Unplugged\n• Turned off\n• Cable damage\nSolutions\n• Check that it is plugged in\n• Turn on the printer's on/off switch\n• Wireless network- check SSID\n28\nPrint Queue Frozen\nCauses\n• Queue blocked\n• Paper jams\n• Low ink or toner\n• Printer malfunction\nSolutions\n• Restart the printer\n• Clear print queue",
