      "content": "The Visible ComputerChapter 2\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nEpisode:Objective(s):Primary PC ComponentsCore 1: 3.0 Hardware\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nEpisode DescriptionMike takes you on a tour of the primary PC components including the computer case, monitor, and various peripherals including the keyboard, mouse, speakers, and more.\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nKey Terms•0:34 - System unit•1:30 - Monitor•1:39 - Keyboard and mouse•1:55 - Printer•2:05 - Speakers•2:19 - Game controller•2:34 - Webcam•2:50 - External hard drive•3:11 - Headset•3:31 - Microphone is for input•3:48 - Microphone\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nQuick Review•The system unit contains the motherboard, CPU, RAM, and hard drives; every other device is a peripheral•Monitors provide visual output and web cameras provide visual input•Keyboards, mice, and game controllers provide input•Printers create paper output•Speakers and headsets make audio output\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nEpisode:Objective(s):Touring a PCCore 1: 3.1 Explain basic cable types and their connectors, features, and purposes.\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nEpisode DescriptionLearn the basic parts of a PC in this episode. \nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nKey Terms•0:35 - Open case (aka open-air frame) and closed case (traditional PC build)•1:28 - Graphics processing unit (GPU)•1:37 - Objective term - Random access memory (RAM) •1:45 - Objective term - Central processing unit (CPU) •3:00 - Mini-DIN (PS/2)•3:09 - Objective term - Universal Serial Bus (USB)•3:09 - Objective term - USB Type-C\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nKey Terms•3:17 - Objective term - High-Definition Multimedia Interface (HDMI)•3:29 - Wi-Fi antenna connectors•3:39 - Audio connectors•3:46 - Input/Output (I/O) shield•4:24 - Objective term - Video Graphics Array (VGA)•4:29 - Objective term - Digital Visual Interface (DVI)•4:55 - Objective term - RJ-45•5:23 - S-Video•5:32 - Expansion slot\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nQuick Review•Knowing what each component and connector is will make you a more efficient technician•Some components, such as USB and audio connectors, utilize unique coloring to enable you to quickly identify the generation\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nEpisode:Objective(s):What Is a Computer?Core 1: 3.3 Given a scenario, select and install storage devices.Core 1: 3.4 Given a scenario, install and configure motherboards, central processing units (CPUs), and add-on cards.\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nEpisode DescriptionComputers are everywhere if you know where to look! What are the parts and the functions of a computer? What do all these devices have in common? \nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nKey Terms•1:30 - Objective term - M.2 SSD•1:32 - Objective term - Hard drive•5:09 - Raspberry Pi\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson\nQuick Review•A computer gets work or play done •A computer will have a CPU, RAM, mass storage, and an operating system •Laptops, mobile devices, and Internet of Things (IoT) devices are all computers\nCompTIA A+ (220-110x)Mike Meyers and Steve Nicholson",
